<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL--Fort Howard rises on bid.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL--Fort Howard rises on bid.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fort Howard Corp shares rose two to 38-1/2 before Monday's U.S. market open on news of the company's merger pact with James River Corp, traders said.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Fort Howard shareholders will receive 1.375 shares of the merged company's common stock for each Fort Howard share, equal to $42.45, or $5.8 billion, including assumption of Fort Howard debt.</p>
<p>The valuation is based on James River's closing stock price of $30.875 on May 2, the companies said.</p>
<p>James River made no moves in early third market trade.</p>
